{title: Danny Boy}
{artist: Traditional}
{key: C}

{c: Verse 1}
Oh [C]Danny [F]boy, the [C]pipes, the [G7]pipes are [C]calling,
From [C]glen to [F]glen, and [D7]down the mountain [G7]side.
The [C]summer's [F]gone, and [C]all the roses [Am]falling,
'Tis [F]you, 'tis [C]you must [G7]go and I must [C]bide.

{c: Verse 2}
But [G7]come ye back when [C]summer's in the [F]meadow,
Or [C]when the valley's [Am]hushed and white with [G7]snow.
'Tis [C]I'll be [F]here in [C]sunshine or in [Am]shadow,
Oh [F]Danny [C]boy, oh [G7]Danny boy, I [C]love you so.

{c: Verse 3}
But [C]when ye [F]come, and [C]all the flowers are [G7]dying,
If [C]I am [F]dead, as [D7]dead I well may [G7]be.
Ye'll [C]come and [F]find the [C]place where I am [Am]lying,
And [F]kneel and [C]say an [G7]Ave there for [C]me.
